 "name": "collatz-10",
 "origin": "programs/collatz.imp",
 "provenance": "krun (K 7.1.337 frontend) on the kdist kimp LLVM definition (kompiled by K v7.1.318, imp-semantics 683a773)",
 "source": "// Port of k-distribution/tests/regression-new/imp-llvm/collatz.imp (K tutorial IMP) to kimp IMP.\n// It tests the Collatz conjecture for all numbers up to m\n// and accumulates the total number of Collatz steps in s.\n// kimp has no declarations, so `int m, n, q, r, s;` becomes explicit zero initialisation.\n// The parameter N is the literal of the line that starts with `m =` (s = 66 when N is 10).\n\nn = 0;\nq = 0;\nr = 0;\ns = 0;\nm = 10;\nwhile (!(m<=2)) {\n  n = m;\n  m = m + -1;\n  while (!(n<=1)) {\n    s = s + 1;\n    q = n/2;\n    r = q+q + 1;\n    if (r<=n) {\n      n = n+n+n + 1;         // n becomes 3*n+1 if odd\n    } else {n=q;}          //        or   n/2 if even\n  }\n}\n"
}
